# To utilize or employ.
## {{sid|en|utilize}} {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[employ]]; to [[apply]]; to [[utilize]].
##: {{ux|en|'''Use''' this knife to slice the bread.}}
##: {{ux|en|We can '''use''' this mathematical formula to solve the problem.}}
##* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2013|month=May-June|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/david-van-tassel David Van Tassel]; [http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/lee-dehaan Lee DeHaan]|title=Wild Plants to the Rescue|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/wild-plants-to-the-rescue|volume=101|issue=3|magazine=w:American Scientist|passage=Plant breeding is always a numbers game. {{...}} The wild species we '''use''' are rich in genetic variation, and individual plants are highly heterozygous and do not breed true. In addition, we are looking for rare alleles, so the more plants we try, the better.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130814191107/http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/feature/2013/3/wild-plants-to-the-rescue|archivedate=14 August 2013}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|often with ''up''}} To [[expend]]; to [[consume]] by employing.
##: {{ux|en|I '''used''' the money they allotted me.}}
##: {{ux|en|We should '''use''' up most of the fuel.}}
##: {{ux|en|She '''used''' all the time allotted to complete the test.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[exploit]].
##: {{ux|en|You never cared about me; you just '''used''' me!}}
##* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=2013|month=September-October|author=[http://www.americanscientist.org/authors/detail/katie-l-burke Katie L. Burke]|magazine=w:American Scientist|title=In the News|url=http://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/5/in-the-news-47|passage=Oxygen levels on Earth skyrocketed 2.4 billion years ago, when cyanobacteria evolved photosynthesis: the ability to convert water and carbon dioxide into carbohydrates and waste oxygen '''using''' solar energy.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130903041000/https://www.americanscientist.org/issues/pub/2013/5/in-the-news-47|archivedate=3 September 2013}}
## {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[consume]] (alcohol, drugs, etc), especially regularly.
##: {{ux|en|He '''uses''' cocaine.}}
##: {{ux|en|I have never '''used''' drugs.}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[consume]] a previously specified [[substance]], especially a [[drug]] to which one is [[addicted]].
##: {{ux|en|Richard began experimenting with cocaine last year; now he '''uses''' almost every day.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|with auxiliary "could"}} To [[benefit]] from; to be able to employ or [[stand]].
##: {{ux|en|I could '''use''' a drink.}}
##: {{ux|en|My car could '''use''' a new coat of paint.}}
## {{lb|en|transitive|with gender pronouns as object}} To [[suggest]] or [[request]] that other people employ a specific set of [[gender]] [[pronoun]]s when referring to the subject.
